From e6c72046e29a9d0a65e2b14871a4ec5972602c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caeliglow-validate <caeliglow@local>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:07:56 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] caeliglow: make external-monitor brightness work out of the
 box

- auto-enable DDC/CI discovery when a Wayland output has a connector but no
  matching sysfs backlight; enable_ddcutil becomes tri-state and still
  overrides in both directions
- in auto mode, ddcutil is authoritative: external monitors reported over
  I2C become controllable even when the compositor does not currently
  expose that connector as a Wayland output (nested sessions, hot-docks);
  an explicit enable_ddcutil preserves the original Wayland-connector filter
- add brightness-rescan msg command that re-runs DDC discovery through the
  same worker path used by enable_ddcutil changes and reports the targets
- add brightness-status msg command that distinguishes no sysfs backlight
  from DDC disabled/undiscovered; clarify that brightness-list-backlight-devices
  is a raw sysfs view, not a health check
- warn once at startup (log + notification) when ~/.config/noctalia exists
  while the caeliglow namespace has no [brightness] config; the old namespace
  is never read or rewritten

Update brightness_service tests for the auto, explicit-false, and
Wayland-unknown-external paths and the user docs for the new commands.
